exit=0
--- stdout ---
Registers the co-located gateway in OAM through the backend, or repairs
an existing registration, and proves the result by exact read-back. The
password is read from a root-only file and streamed to the backend on
stdin — never through a flag value, argv, or the environment.

Examples:
  loxicmd appliance gateway register-local --username admin --password-file /etc/loxilb-appliance/oam.pass

Usage:
  loxicmd appliance gateway register-local [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                   help for register-local
      --password-file string   Root-only (0600) file holding the OAM password; a literal password option does not exist by design
      --username string        OAM username to register with

Global Flags:
  -s, --apiserver string   Set API server IP address (default "127.0.0.1")
      --bearer             Send the token as 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' (required by the inference gateway; disable for classic loxilb raw-token targets) (default true)
      --cacert string      CA certificate (PEM) to verify the server (https only)
      --cert string        Client certificate (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -k, --insecure           Skip TLS certificate verification (https only)
      --key string         Client private key (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -o, --output string      Set output layer (ex.) wide, json)
  -p, --port int           Set API server port number (default 11111)
      --protocol string    Set API server http/https (default "http")
  -t, --timeout int16      Set timeout (default 10)
      --token string       Set Token for the API server
--- stderr ---
